      "paper": {
        "submissionId": "USSTC26-ABS-0142",
        "title": "Low-Cost IoT Sensor Network for Early Landslide Warning in Uttarakhand Hill Districts",
        "abstractText": "Landslides cause recurring loss of life and property in the hill districts of Uttarakhand, particularly during the monsoon. This study presents a low-cost early warning network built from soil-moisture, tilt and rain-gauge sensors connected over LoRaWAN to a cloud dashboard. A pilot of twelve sensor nodes was installed on two slopes with a history of slope failure. A threshold model combining cumulative rainfall and pore-water indicators raised alerts on average 40 minutes before observed slope movement, with a hardware cost below INR 6,000 per node. The results suggest that community-maintained sensor networks can complement regional forecasting and support timely evacuation in remote villages.",
        "abstractNote": null,
